  <article class="docs-content">
    <section class="docs-hero" id="overview">
      <p class="eyebrow">Documentation · v2.3.1</p>
      <h2>Run your own support workspace.</h2>
      <p>EasySupport is a self-hosted Discord bot with a web dashboard for tickets, moderation, automod, logging, and guild workflows.</p>
      <div class="docs-hero__actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="#quickstart">Start setup <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="<%= repoUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="quickstart">
      <p class="eyebrow">Quickstart</p>
      <h3>From clone to running bot.</h3>
      <div class="docs-steps">
        <div class="docs-step"><strong>01</strong><div><h4>Install dependencies</h4><p>Use Node.js 22.5 or newer, then install the project packages.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Marcel1kub1/EasySupport.git
cd EasySupport
npm install</code></pre></div></div>
        <div class="docs-step"><strong>02</strong><div><h4>Create your environment</h4><p>Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> and fill in the values below.</p></div></div>
        <div class="docs-step"><strong>03</strong><div><h4>Start the service</h4><p>Run the bot and website together from the project root.</p><pre><code>npm start</code></pre></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="requirements">
      <p class="eyebrow">Deployment</p>
      <h3>What you need first.</h3>
      <div class="docs-card-grid">
        <div class="docs-card"><span class="docs-card__icon">JS</span><h4>Node.js 22.5+</h4><p>The runtime required by the bot and its native test tooling.</p></div>
        <div class="docs-card"><span class="docs-card__icon">DB</span><h4>MySQL database</h4><p>A database the bot can use to store guild settings, tickets, and transcripts.</p></div>
        <div class="docs-card"><span class="docs-card__icon">DC</span><h4>Discord application</h4><p>A bot token, application ID, OAuth secret, and the correct redirect URL.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="environment">
      <p class="eyebrow">Configuration</p>
      <h3>Fill in <code>.env</code>.</h3>
      <p>Keep this file on your server only. Never commit real tokens, passwords, or session secrets.</p>
      <pre class="docs-code"><code>DISCORD_TOKEN=your-bot-token
CLIENT_ID=your-application-id
CLIENT_SECRET=your-oauth-client-secret

MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
MYSQL_PORT=3306
MYSQL_USER=easysupport
MYSQL_PASSWORD=your-database-password
MYSQL_DATABASE=easysupport

PORT=3000
SESSION_SECRET=use-a-long-random-secret
OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-domain.example/auth/callback</code></pre>
      <div class="docs-callout"><strong>Important:</strong> Use the exact variable names from <code>.env.example</code>. The production <code>.env</code> is private; only the example belongs in the repository.</div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="run">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start the service</p>
      <h3>Launch and keep it online.</h3>
      <p>For a server deployment, use a process manager such as systemd or PM2 so the bot restarts after reboots and failures.</p>
      <pre><code>npm start
# or
pm2 start src/index.js --name easysupport
pm2 save</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="discord">
      <p class="eyebrow">Discord setup</p>
      <h3>Connect the application.</h3>
      <ol class="docs-list">
        <li>Create an application in the Discord Developer Portal.</li>
        <li>Create a bot, copy its token into <code>DISCORD_TOKEN</code>, and enable the intents used by the project.</li>
        <li>Add the OAuth redirect URL from <code>OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI</code> to the application settings.</li>
        <li>Invite the bot with the permissions required for tickets, messages, roles, and moderation.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="dashboard">
      <p class="eyebrow">Dashboard setup</p>
      <h3>Configure your guild.</h3>
      <p>Open <code>/login</code>, authorize Discord, choose a guild you manage, and configure modules from the dashboard. Changes are saved per guild and protected by the dashboard session.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" id="troubleshooting">
      <p class="eyebrow">Troubleshooting</p>
      <h3>Common setup checks.</h3>
      <div class="docs-faq">
        <details open><summary>The bot exits with a missing environment variable</summary><p>Compare your server <code>.env</code> with <code>.env.example</code>. Required values include the Discord credentials, all MySQL values, and <code>OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI</code>.</p></details>
        <details><summary>The website cannot connect to MySQL</summary><p>Confirm the database is running, the credentials are correct, and the database user can connect from the bot server.</p></details>
        <details><summary>OAuth redirects back with an error</summary><p>The redirect URI must match exactly in Discord and in <code>OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI</code>, including protocol, hostname, path, and port.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</div>
